SUMMARY:Experimental/Behavioural – Maroš Servátka (Macquarie) – Coord
 ination in altruistic markets with imperfect substitutes and restricted de
 mand
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Maroš Servátka: “Coordination in altruistic markets with im
 perfect substitutes and restricted demand”\nhttps://sites.google.com/sit
 e/marosservatka/\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2
 ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAGG.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo
 .gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nCharitable giving and volunteering pro
 vide essential goods and services where governments fall short\, yet altru
 istic markets often suffer from coordination failures. We study how decent
 ralized altruistic choice generates inefficiencies in markets with imperfe
 ctly substitutable goods. In a laboratory experiment\, subjects choose bet
 ween providing an altruistic good with a relatively high recipient benefit
  but limited demand\, providing an alternative altruistic good with a lowe
 r benefit and unlimited demand\, or not helping. Across treatments\, we va
 ry the recipient benefit of the alternative good. Consistent with theoreti
 cal predictions\, we find prevalent oversupply of the preferred good in th
 e absence of the alternative good and when the alternative good is clearly
  inferior but prevalent undersupply of the preferred good when the alterna
 tive good generates sufficient recipient benefit. These patterns predictab
 ly emerge from donors’ trade-offs between recipient impact and the risk 
 that contributions will be wasted\, generating substantial welfare losses 
 despite ample aggregate willingness to help. A simple coordination device 
 that informs donors when demand for the preferred good is saturated and re
 directs excess contributions to the alternative good significantly improve
 s market efficiency\, reducing both over- and undersupply.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAG
 G.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
